messages:
liz: Heads up — ACME reported a streaming hang with the TS SDK. Connection stays open but no onmessage events after first few bytes, iterator never yields final event.
ajay: Do we have request ids / logs?
liz: request_id=rid_8f3c, trace shows HTTP 200 then a chunked response where the blank line delimiter between events is split across network frames. Looks like our parser never emits the event when the final CRLFCRLF arrives in a subsequent chunk.
kevin: That sounds like the parser assumes the event boundary is in the same chunk. Can you paste a minimal repro?
liz: Minimal server (node):
```js
// minimal SSE server that splits delimiter across chunks
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req,res)=>{
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' });
  res.write('data: part-1'); // no newlines yet
  setTimeout(()=>{
    res.write('\n\n'); // delimiter arrives later
    // keep connection open
  }, 30);
}).listen(9000);
```
Client (TS SDK EventSource polyfill):
```ts
const es = new EventSource('http://localhost:9000');
es.onmessage = (e)=>console.log('msg', e.data);
es.onerror = (e)=>console.error('err', e);
// result: no 'msg' logged, connection stays open
```
ajay: Reproduced locally. Our polyfill's line parser short-circuits when it doesn't find a full line in the current buffer and drops partial buffer when next chunk arrives.
tara: Is this a regression? any PRs touching the SSE parser recently?
kevin: Looks like PR #8921 changed parsing to use a single-regex match on incoming chunk instead of incremental state machine — that would break when delimiter straddles chunks.
liz: Customer impact: production stream stuck for ~40s and app-level timeouts kicked in. Marking P1 and escalating to eng-runtime.
support-bot: Ticket created: #INC-10245 — assigned to eng-runtime. Notifying oncall.
ajay: Quick mitigation: suggest wrapper that buffers until you see "\n\n" before handing lines to the parser. I'll draft a hotfix patch for the polyfill.
kevin: Two options — revert PR #8921 or add incremental buffering + unit tests to cover split-delimiter cases. Revert may be faster.
tara: Can we ship a patch to main + cherry-pick to stable v1.x? Customer is on v1.3.2.
kevin: I'll cut a revert branch now, run unit tests, and open a backport PR. ETA ~90m.
liz: Thanks — pls post the hotfix PR number here when ready and include repro script so support can validate with ACME.
ajay: Also adding an integration test that simulates chunk boundaries at random positions to catch regressions.
kevin: PR opened: #8939 (revert parser change) and #8940 (backport to v1.x). Will monitor rolling deploy. :rocket:
liz: ACME verified that messages resumed after we rolled the revert to staging; waiting on prod deploy. Keeping ticket open until prod confirmed. :heavy_check_mark:
